      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is error here is due to the fact that we have two entries for the CellIdentityGsm object, the constructor and the Parcel. We have strict rules on MCC/MNC to exclude null, empty string and not 3-digits input in our constructor. But when we convert a Parcel to CellIdentity, we didn\u0027t have corresponding rules. (reference: https://cs.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/opt/telephony/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/RIL.java?rcl\u003d4d7052fe42d19be0bf71b55d3c69196f4d8ffec7\u0026l\u003d4925)\n\nSo I made the following two changes here:\n1. handle the case that MCC/MNC could be empty string in the constructor (it could happen if read from Parcel).\n2. Use the same constructor when construct from Parcel.",
